Comment: This is the binary package's copyright file.
 incant's own code is BSD-3-Clause. The package also bundles, in the Python
 virtual environment under /usr/lib/incant/venv, third-party Python packages
 and the native libraries inside their wheels. With the default extras
 (kokoro mobi) these include GPL-3.0 components that incant loads in-process:
 mobi 0.4.x (GPL-3.0-only), phonemizer (GPL-3.0-or-later) and espeakng-loader,
 which bundles libespeak-ng and espeak-ng-data (GPL-3.0-or-later). The package
 as a whole is therefore distributed under the terms of the GNU GPL version 3,
 while incant's own files remain under BSD-3-Clause and can be reused under it.
 .
 Every bundled component, its version and its license are listed in
 /usr/share/doc/incant/THIRD_PARTY_NOTICES.md. License texts are in each
 package's dist-info directory under
 /usr/lib/incant/venv/lib/python3.*/site-packages/ and, for components that do
 not ship one (and for the GPL/LGPL/MPL family), in
 /usr/share/doc/incant/LICENSES/. THIRD_PARTY_NOTICES.md also says how to obtain
 the Corresponding Source of the GPL, LGPL and MPL components.

